 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"fig9_11\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/d3ada30a48bbc4a7.png\" alt=\"The cartoon shows Boss Tweed leaning on a voting booth that is labeled In Counting There is Strength. The booth has the ballot box on top of it. The caption at the bottom of the cartoon reads “‘That’s what’s the matter.’ Boss Tweed: ‘As long as I count the votes, what are you going to do about it? Say?’”\">\n<figcaption>The text in this political cartoon from 1871 reads, “The Ballot. In Counting There Is Strength.” The text beneath the image reads, “That’s What’s The Matter.” Boss Tweed. “’As long as I count the votes, what are you going to do about it? Say?’”</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615670,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The context illustrated by the political cartoon was",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170648,
     "content_html": "Jim Crow laws preventing African Americans from voting in the South"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170649,
     "content_html": "corrupt elections in major cities run by political machines"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170647,
     "content_html": "large industries controlling the vote"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170646,
     "content_html": "farmers losing their majority in the House of Representatives"
    }
   ],
